Derived from that project:

  hooks/always-on.mjs
      Direct port. Two deliberate changes: the opt-in flag check is removed
      (the standard is unconditional here), and failure is loud instead of
      silent. The file carries an attribution header.

  standard/INTERACTION-STANDARD.md
      Rules F1, F9, F10 and F11 are adopted from that project's rules R10
      (first half), R5, R6 and R8; F2, F5 (step economy), F7 and F12 are
      adapted from R1, R2, R9 and R7. R10 (for the F13 block only) and the
      opt-in trigger are deliberately overridden; R1 and R3 are kept. The
      reasoning is in skills/interaction-standard/reference/provenance.md.

  evals/
      Rubric structure (weighted dimensions, blocking findings, baseline
      comparison) follows that project's approach.
